      "Control": "Avoid handling wild animals or strays. Contact a veterinarian upon observing a wild animal or a stray, especially if the animal is acting strangely. Vaccinate dogs against Rabies. Puppies at the age of 12 weeks (3 months) to be a given a single dose 1 ml of a killed vaccine (SC or IM). Adult dogs with an unknown history of vaccination be given a single dose 1ml of a killed vaccine (SC or IM), a booster given a year later and thereafter, vaccination performed every three years by the vaccine approved for three year administration. Cattle and sheep at the age of above 12 months are vaccinated at a dose of 2ml IM. Annual revaccination is recommended"
