      "Transmission": "The intermediate host for Moniezia, is a mite which lives in damp grass. The mite ingests the eggs and then is accidentally swallowed by the calf, kid or lamb. Since these young animals will start licking grass at an early age, they can be infected very early in life. It is possible for a 6 week old calf to be infected by an adult tapeworm and already passing eggs. The passed segments can be seen in the dung looking like grains of rice.",
